      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You can already do something like that in 2 ways:\n-By enabling-disabling the relative object\n-using the Behaviour.enabled keyframe inside an animation.\n\nThe second one is a bit of an \"hacked in\" way to do it since the option is not available in the animation editor right away (i personally copy the keyframe from another animation that has it), but it works, and has enabled a lot of people to do entire inventories on their avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
