  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-19T18:45:59.395Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, my idea is for VRChat to make an Script for us to be able to activate/deactivate an Animator with an controller that has an Animation attached through an Animation/Gesture/Emote.\nI read on several locations you will need a script to be able to activate an Animator from Off position to On.\n\nSo the fault we have now is that Animator's in Unity have to stay Active to be able to be used, this creates an reduced usability of the Component for us Avatar creators without access to Triggers/Other Scripts.\nSo by being able to activate an Animator through an Animation by having the Animation activate an script linked to an Animator you can at hand keep the Game object Active and change the animation for the Game Object/Avatar at will.\n\nSince having long animations on a Gesture does not work and Emotes makes you stay still for the period of animation.\nAnimators makes it possible to create lots of fun stuff and will create an whole new level of interactions for the community.\n\nExamples of usage:\n1. Changing the animation of an GameObject you are currently using without having to deactivate and activate an new GameObject. (Less use of meshes , animations and GameObjects)\n\n2. Activate Props Through Emotes. (The animator - Animation keeps itself active through the script, until Game object is deactivated through another Emote).\n\n3. Change animation sets through Emotes  (Same as No. 2)",
